        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThis is an intended and [documented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/35422e90b0de232245e2b1d3b3737a7c419d377b/doc/mini-splitjoin.txt#L478-L482) behavior. The idea is that it is consistent with common case of splitting function call (like `f(a, b, c)`) or an array without initial padding (like `[a, b, c]`).\r\n\r\nThe suggested way to account for that is indeed with custom hooks.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
